# Tele-trouncing (P1 arrows) callout drops: the two findOrWaitForBuff waits split
# the player's arrow buffs on a hard 8.5s initial-duration boundary, set 1 ~7s vs
# set 2 ~10s. On some pulls one side of the split never matched, the ttSq
# invocation burned its whole 180s budget waiting, and every TT callout after
# the initial 'Arrows' silently vanished for the pull (verified in sidecar logs:
# SequentialTriggerTimeoutException at DMU.java findOrWaitForBuff, exactly 180s
# after the Arrows call, twice in one raid night). The waits now take the
# player's two arrow buffs in any order and sort by initial duration, shorter
# resolves first, so duration jitter cannot strand the chain. If no arrow buff
# ever lands the trigger speaks its existing TT: Error callout and logs every
# arrow-id buff in the state at ERROR, which distinguishes a missing 26-line
# feed (empty list) from an isThePlayer mismatch (other players listed).
# Against the event-trigger pin in build.sh, after dmu-crash-guards.patch. Upstream candidate.
